CONFIGS: vfrot 0.8_1_2_0.94 (beta 0.8, add 1 Gbit/s per s, T 2 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000), vfrot 0.8_1_2_0.94_B12000 (beta 0.8, add 1 Gbit/s per s, T 2 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 12000), vfrot 0.8_1_2_0.94_B20000 (beta 0.8, add 1 Gbit/s per s, T 2 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 20000), vfrot 0.9_1_2_0.94 (beta 0.9, add 1 Gbit/s per s, T 2 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000), vfrot 0.8_2_2_0.94 (beta 0.8, add 2 Gbit/s per s, T 2 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000), vfrot 0.8_1_1_0.94 (beta 0.8, add 1 Gbit/s per s, T 1 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000), vffair 0.8_1_2_0.94_F0.5 (beta 0.8, add 1 Gbit/s per s, T 2 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000, floor 0.5 x B / n_active), vffair 0.8_1_2_0.94_F0.25 (beta 0.8, add 1 Gbit/s per s, T 2 s, thresh 0.94, BMAX 16000, floor 0.25 x B / n_active)
REFERENCE CONFIG for the paired summary: vfrot 0.8_1_2_0.94 (identical to exp39 vfrot)
TOKEN BUCKET: all modes use the same xdp_limit.o on every flooder interface, burst 5 ms at the cap rate; victim interfaces never limited (counter only)
VICTIMS: V1 = tenant1 10.10.0.11 port 5201, V2 = tenant5 10.10.0.15 port 5205, each 9 Gbit/s, one stream, constant for [0,40) s (launched together 0.5 s after the flooders); slo_ok per victim = fraction of its 39 1 s windows >= 95% of its own per-repeat reference; slo_ok_worst = the smaller of the two
VICTIM CMD V1: ssh alpine@10.10.0.11 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5201 -t 40 -b 9G -J'
VICTIM CMD V2: ssh alpine@10.10.0.15 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5205 -t 40 -b 9G -J'
FLOODER CMD A: ssh alpine@10.10.0.12 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5202 -t 28 -P 2 -J'
FLOODER CMD B: ssh alpine@10.10.0.13 'sleep 6; iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5203 -t 28 -P 2 -J'
FLOODER CMD C: ssh alpine@10.10.0.14 'sleep 12; iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5204 -t 28 -P 2 -J'
FLOODER CMD D: ssh alpine@10.10.0.16 'sleep 18; iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5206 -t 22 -P 2 -J'
REF CMD V1: ssh alpine@10.10.0.11 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5201 -t 10 -b 9G -J' (both together, 2 runs)
REF CMD V2: ssh alpine@10.10.0.15 'iperf3 -c 10.10.0.1 -p 5205 -t 10 -b 9G -J' (both together, 2 runs)
vfrot: feedback = WORST victim, min over V1/V2 of EMA(1 s rate)/own reference < thresh; budget start 10000, clamp [800, BMAX] Mbit/s (BMAX 16000 unless a B suffix), rotation over 4 holders (holder gets B - (n_active - 1) x 200)
vffair: as vfrot (same budget law, same holder = lowest delivered since all active, same rotation), but every ACTIVE non-holder gets floor = max(200, F x B / n_active) and the holder B - (n_active - 1) x floor (one active: B - 200); inactive flooders keep 200 outside the budget, as vfrot
METRICS: flooder_total = sum of the eBPF means; min_flooder_own = smallest eBPF mean over each flooder's own window; min_flooder_ovl = smallest rate over the all-active window 18-28 s; budget_ceiling/floor_share = share of all ticks of the slot with budget >= BMAX / <= 800; highcapX_share = share of ticks in 18-28 s with capX >= 0.5 x budget; Jain over the eBPF rates in the all-active window (as exp39)
HOST CPU: /proc/stat aggregate line, busy % = 1 - (idle + iowait)/total as exp37 (total = sum of all fields); steal % = steal field / same total (reported by this kernel); host CPUs: nproc 6, os.cpu_count() 6; tick length = time between consecutive reads of tenant1's counter (nominal 0.25 s), WARNING if a slot's mean > 0.3 s (first tick, which spans the launch, excluded) or its steal mean > 1% or max > 5%
EXPECTED DURATION: 17 slots/repeat, ~15.1 min/repeat (exp39 measured rate ~14.5), 6 repeats + 5 x 600 s rest ~ 2.34 h (measured rate ~2.28 h)
